CORE
main.c
--unwind 2 --rounds 2 --por --allow-pointer-unsoundness --no-assertions --datarace
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
`pa->id = ++uid` inside an atomic section, with `pa = &th[i]`, while main
writes `pb->op`, `pb = &th[j]`, j != i. The store loads th[i] at the
undecided index, and that load reads element k under `i == k`
(shared_read_cond). Inside an atomic section l2_thread_read_encoding dropped
that condition, so the load was recorded as reading every element of `th`
and paired with main's write of th[j].op: a race no execution has. The same
program without the atomic section was already SUCCESSFUL.

Reported FAILED before the fix, SUCCESSFUL after. Reduced from
pthread-complex/elimination_backoff_stack (no-data-race).

See `atomic_section_element_store_race`: i == j and both write `id`, which
must stay FAILED.
